# Line endings: developed on Windows, deployed on Linux (Render, containers,
# bash). Git must store LF in the repository for text files, or a CRLF
# `scripts/build_web.sh`, Dockerfile or nginx.conf reaches Linux and breaks:
#   bash: $'\r': command not found
#   nginx: [emerg] unknown directive "server\r"
# `* text=auto eol=lf` normalises every text file to LF in the repo *and* checks
# it out as LF, so a Windows working copy can never reintroduce CRLF in a commit.
# (Binary files are unaffected: `text=auto` only applies to content git detects
# as text.)
* text=auto eol=lf

# The committed Flutter web bundle is generated output — never rewrite its bytes.
frontend/build/web/** -text

# Fonts and images in the bundle are binary, and so is anything else git would
# otherwise guess wrong about.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.wasm binary
